refused: d223_stderr_then_stored.cy:7:5, line 7 column 5
 7 |     std::io::fmt_print.stderr.stored("{}{newln}", $tenth);
   |     ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
 fix:  `std::io::fmt_print.stored.stderr`
 why:  the narrowing that changes the action most sits next to the thing, and `.stored` changes what's printed while `.stderr` changes only where (D223)
